# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# Generated dashboards / galleries (regenerate from deck lists + collection)
*-dashboard.html
*-visual.html
dashboard.html

# The player's live collection export is theirs — keep the private full CSV out of
# git by default. The name-only snapshot (data/collection/collection_snapshot.txt)
# IS committed as a fallback. Uncomment the next line if you'd rather commit the CSV.
data/collection/collection.csv
data/collection/*.private.csv

# Scratch
scratch/
*.tmp

# Generated dashboards (regenerate with scripts/refresh.py)
build/

# Derived card-attribute enrichment (regenerate with carddb.py from a Scryfall bulk file)
data/collection/collection_attrs.csv

# TEMPORARY — REMOVE THIS LINE when the attrs-snapshot Action lands.
# This path is *meant* to be committed (docs/spec-network-and-attrs.md §3), but ONLY
# ever written by that Action. It is ignored in the interim because the file keeps
# reappearing as scratch output from review subagents, and on 2026-08-12 one such stub
# (2,621 identical "Creature/MV 3/Elf" rows) was committed and made every deck read as
# 100 cards at MV 3 with zero lands — silently, since the honesty labels only fire on
# MISSING data, never on wrong data. Ignoring it is the cheap guard until the Action —
# with the row-count AND plausibility checks in §6a — is the only writer.
data/collection/collection_attrs.snapshot.csv

# Scryfall bulk cache (large; auto-downloaded by carddb.py)
data/collection/scryfall-*.json
data/collection/scryfall-*.json.part

# Cached third-party data (EDHREC / CSB) — derived, regenerate on demand
data/cache/

# Windows crash dumps
*.stackdump
